{{!
    @template local_uckk/status_badge

    Renders a canonical UCKK status badge.

    This template is display-only. Status validation, class mapping,
    capability checks, visibility rules, and language string selection must be
    handled by PHP renderables/services before rendering.

    Classes required for JS:
    * none

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-status

    Context variables required for this template:
    * status - Canonical status value, for example "active".
    * label - Localised visible label.
    * statusclass - Safe CSS modifier class generated by PHP.

    Context variables optional for this template:
    * description - Localised accessible description.
    * sizeclass - Safe CSS size modifier class generated by PHP.
    * extraclasses - Safe additional classes generated by PHP.
    * iconclass - Safe icon class generated by PHP.
    * showicon - Whether to render the visual icon.
    * muted - Whether to render the badge as secondary/muted.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "status": "active",
        "label": "Active",
        "description": "This item is active and visible to authorised users.",
        "statusclass": "uckk-status-badge--active",
        "sizeclass": "uckk-status-badge--sm",
        "extraclasses": "",
        "iconclass": "fa fa-circle-check",
        "showicon": true,
        "muted": false
    }
}}

<span
    class="uckk-status-badge {{statusclass}}{{#sizeclass}} {{sizeclass}}{{/sizeclass}}{{#muted}} uckk-status-badge--muted{{/muted}}{{#extraclasses}} {{extraclasses}}{{/extraclasses}}"
    data-status="{{status}}"
    {{#description}}title="{{description}}" aria-label="{{description}}"{{/description}}
    {{^description}}aria-label="{{label}}"{{/description}}
>
    {{#showicon}}
        <span class="uckk-status-badge__icon {{iconclass}}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    {{/showicon}}

    <span class="uckk-status-badge__label">{{label}}</span>
</span>